Revision history for Web-VWF

0.004.1	Mon Nov 23 08:02:40 PM EST 2026
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- A missing default databases directory is no longer an error: it is logged at notice
	and no data driver is loaded; one the site names is still an error.

0.004.0	Mon Nov 23 01:51:09 PM EST 2026
	[ Incompatible changes ]
	- The data files and the drivers that read them are now configured apart:
	<databases><directory> is where the data files (CSV, XML, SQLite) are
	(replacing database_dir, which is still read), and <data> declares the drivers,
	one <driver> each, with a <directory> for all of them or for one.  Without a
	directory the drivers are looked for in the databases directory, then @INC,
	rather than only in @INC; only the <directory> of a <driver> is strict, the others
	fall back to @INC.  <databases><database> is no longer read (a warning is logged);
	write <data><driver>.  The example site's states driver is in example/data/ and its data
	files in example/databases/.  The default databases directory is now
	../databases, not ../data, which is for the drivers.

	[ Enhancements ]
	- Documented the six functions in Web::VWF that pod-coverage reported:
	sig_handler, choose, send_error, duration_seconds, blacklisted and filter.
	- Makefile.PL's META_MERGE excludes example/ and Data::Throttler::Backend::VWF
	from the PAUSE index.

	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- Choose the right Perl in the example/cgi-bin/page.fcgi

0.003.1	Thu Nov 19 08:14:20 PM EST 2026
	[ Enhancements ]
	- Web::VWF loads CGI::Alert, so an error that stops a page script is emailed
	to the server administrator (the SERVER_ADMIN setting, or webmaster@localhost
	when the web server has not set one).
	- example/cgi-bin/page.fcgi shows how a site that keeps its modules in a
	private directory (cpanm -l ~/perl5, local::lib) sets @INC: in a BEGIN block
	that comes first in the script, with lib->import, so that the compiled
	modules in the architecture directory are found and autodie cannot load the
	system List::Util before the newer one.

	[ Bug fixes ]
	- A site with no SERVER_ADMIN, such as a FastCGI worker started by
	mod_fcgid, no longer logs "Use of uninitialized value" warnings from
	CGI::Alert every time it starts, which also made the B::Lint and
	warnings::unused checks of page.fcgi fail.

0.003.0	Tue Nov 17 12:05:14 PM EST 2026
	[ Enhancements ]
	- The pages a site serves are declared in <display>, one <page> element for
	each, with a <name> and a <description> (shown in the 300 response).  A
	<directory> in <display> or in a <page> says where the page modules are, instead
	of @INC; with no <page>, the modules found in the <display> directory are the
	pages.  The old <pages> setting, and its string of names, is still read.
	- The data modules a site loads are declared in <databases>, one <database>
	element for each, with a <name>, a <description> and a <directory> likewise.
	A name with no :: in it is a Web::VWF::Data:: module, so <name>states</name> is
	Web::VWF::Data::states.  The old <data_modules> string is still read.  (It is
	not called <data> because Database::Abstraction takes constructor arguments
	from top-level configuration keys, and data is one of them.)
	- File-based caches (Berkeley DB, File) now go in $CACHEDIR, or failing that
	$CACHE_DIR, when either is set, ahead of $root_dir and the configuration; the
	directory is created if it does not exist.  Previously root_dir=example put
	CGI+3a+3aLingua, __db.* and the rest inside example/.
	- The example site has a states page (?page=states), reading
	example/data/states.csv (the 50 U.S. states) through Web::VWF::Data::states,
	Web::VWF::Display::states and states.tmpl, which are in example/lib; and
	example/data/index.csv, the people the contact form can reach.
	- Documented every site setting: a new CONFIGURATION section in the Web::VWF
	POD and the README, with the defaults.  Added the SYNOPSIS and run() to the
	POD, POD for every module, Web::VWF::Utils::env_cache_dir, an AUTHOR and a
	LICENCE section for each, and a LICENSE file.
	- t/pod-coverage.t (an author test) checks that every public subroutine is
	documented, and t/version.t no longer skips a Changes entry that has no date
	yet when checking its version (the date is required under RELEASE_TESTING),
	and checks the example site's modules too.
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- Require HTML::D3 0.30.  CPAN Testers (Perl 5.44, aarch64 Linux) had 0.23 and
	the meta_data page, t/function.t and t/meta-data-charts.t died with "Data must
	be an array of arrays": 0.23 takes render_pie_chart_snippet($data, $opts)
	positionally, and meta_data passes a hash.  The prerequisite is now declared in
	Makefile.PL, cpanfile and linux.yml, and meta_data checks it on load.
	Fixes https://matrix.perl-magpie.org/results/ffb3469e-de40-11f1-a09d-aafb97416a10
	- Handle captcha display failure
	- The POD of Blacklist, Utils and Config still used the old VWF:: names, so
	its SYNOPSIS did not load.
	- Data::Throttler::Backend::VWF, which Web::VWF::Throttle defines in another
	distribution's namespace, is no longer offered to PAUSE (no_index).
	- Declared Test::Needs, which t/pod.t uses, and recommend Mail::DKIM and
	Crypt::OpenSSL::RSA for the tests that sign a message.
	- ASCII only in the source of Web::VWF; one line indented with spaces now uses tabs.

0.002.0	Wed Nov 11 08:54:17 PM EST 2026
	[ Enhancements ]
	- Added Web::VWF::Mail: sends mail through sendmail(1), signed with DKIM when
	the site configures DKIMSelector and DKIMKey.  Mail::DKIM is recommended,
	not required; without it, or without a key, mail is sent unsigned.
	Web::VWF::Display::index now sends through it.
	- Mail rejects a sender that could be read as a sendmail option or a header.
	- Declared the dependencies that were only loaded lazily and so were missing
	from the build files: Data::Validate::URI, DateTime, LWP::Simple::WithCache,
	Time::Duration::Parse, XML::LibXML and YAML.
	- Debug logging of the configuration now redacts secrets, keys and tokens
	(Web::VWF::Utils::redact_config).
	- Every module now carries the distribution's $VERSION.
	- Documented the API of new(), and of Web::VWF::Mail.
	- Corrected the README and POD, which described a site layout that is not in
	the distribution, and fixed 8-space indentation in two modules.
	- Declared the licence as GPL2 in the metadata, and kept example/ and t/ out
	of the CPAN index.

0.001.0	Tue Nov 10 09:00:49 PM EST 2026
	First draft
